<title>USA: US Home Builders-Market Index falls to 51 in Nov.</title>
<headline>US Home Builders-Market Index falls to 51 in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Home Builders said its Housing Market Index fell four points to 51 in November from a revised 55 in October.</p>
<p>Builders' ratings of single-family home sales fell to 54 in November from 59 in October. Traffic of prospective buyers fell to 40 from 44. The component index for single family sales in the next 6 months fell to 58 from 62, it said.</p>
<p>A Housing Market Index over 50 generally means the number of positive responses received from builders exceeded the number of negative responses. The October index is based on the ratings of 373 respondents.  </p>
